###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#misogynous_stereotype
:misogynous_stereotype rdf:type :BackgroundKnowledge ;
                rdfs:label "Misogynous Stereotype"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The meme expresses extreme hatred toward women, which relies on the real-world concept of misogyny — a systemic prejudice and discrimination against women. This includes stereotypes that women are irrational, emotional, or less competent, which the meme implicitly invokes by using hateful language and framing it as a serious declaration."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "69085.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-19T10:17:12.509581" .

###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dog_snarl_as_aggression_metaphor
:dog_snarl_as_aggression_metaphor rdf:type :BackgroundKnowledge ;
                rdfs:label "Dog Snarl as Aggression Metaphor"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The visual of the dog snarling is used as a metaphor for rage or hostility. This relies on the real-world understanding that dogs displaying such expressions are perceived as aggressive, which is then mapped onto the hateful text to amplify the message. This is a common meme trope where animal expressions are used to convey human emotions or attitudes."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "69085.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-19T10:17:12.509581" .

###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#bro_culture
:bro_culture rdf:type :BackgroundKnowledge ;
                rdfs:label "Bro Culture"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The phrase 'i'm not even joking bro' is a colloquial expression often used in 'bro culture' — a social trend among young men that emphasizes machismo, hyper-masculinity, and the use of casual, often dismissive or aggressive language. This cultural context is necessary to understand the tone and intent of the meme, as it frames the statement as a serious, unironic declaration from a male perspective."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "69085.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-19T10:17:12.509581" .

###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#hateful_meme_format
:hateful_meme_format rdf:type :BackgroundKnowledge ;
                rdfs:label "Hateful Meme Format"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The format of the meme — pairing an image of an aggressive animal with hateful text — is a known trope in internet culture used to express extreme views in a seemingly 'serious' or 'authentic' way. This format relies on the audience's understanding of meme conventions and the use of visual metaphors to convey toxic messages, which is a real-world cultural phenomenon."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "69085.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-19T10:17:12.509581" .

###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#hatred
:hatred rdf:type :Emotion ;
                rdfs:label "hateful emotion"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The emotion of intense dislike or animosity toward women, explicitly stated in the text overlay and amplified by the aggressive visual metaphor of the snarling dog."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "69085.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-19T10:17:12.509581" .

###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#mapping_1
:mapping_1 rdf:type :AnalogicalMapping ;
                rdfs:label "Dog's aggressive expression mapped to the speaker's hatred"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The visual of the Shiba Inu dog snarling with its mouth open and teeth bared is mapped onto the textual statement 'i hate women so much'. The dog's aggressive expression serves as a visual metaphor for the speaker's supposed rage or hostility toward women, amplifying the hateful message through the common meme trope of using animal aggression to represent human emotion. This mapping relies on the audience's understanding that the dog's expression conveys anger, which is then analogically projected onto the speaker's stated emotion."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "69085.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-19T10:17:12.509581" .

###  http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1
:semiotic_projection_1 rdf:type :SemioticProjection ;
                rdfs:label "User projected onto the dog's aggressive expression as a metaphor for their own hatred"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "The user is projecting themselves onto the visual material of the Shiba Inu dog snarling, interpreting the dog's aggressive expression as a metaphor for their own stated hatred toward women. The meme format uses the dog's expression to visually represent the user's internal state, creating a semiotic projection where the user identifies with the dog's perceived rage. This projection is reinforced by the textual material 'i hate women so much' and 'i'm not even joking bro', which frames the user's identity as the speaker of this hateful declaration."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "69085.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-19T10:17:12.509581" .

